# Build output
#
# Patterns are anchored rather than global: they name the solution-wide and
# per-project output directories explicitly, so a vendored dependency that
# happens to ship an x64/ or Release/ directory of its own is never swept up.
# gitignore cannot re-include anything under an excluded directory, so a bare
# `x64/` would make such files vanish silently.

# Solution-wide output
/x64/
/Win32/
/Release/
/Debug/

# Per-project output: one path component then the build dir, so nothing nested
# deeper than a project directory is matched.
*/x64/
*/Win32/
*/Release/
*/Debug/

# Visual Studio's per-project "unique intermediate directory"
*/Jungle L.*/

# .NET
*/obj/
*/bin/
project.assets.json
*.nuget.g.props
*.nuget.g.targets

# Visual Studio
.vs/
*.user
*.suo
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates
*.VC.db
*.VC.VC.opendb

# Build artefacts that escape the directories above
*.obj
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.idb
*.exp
*.tlog
*.log
*.aps

# Claude Code: machine-specific tool permissions, not useful to anyone else
.claude/settings.local.json

# OS
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store
